raph above, solve the inequality $(x + 2)(x - 3) \\ge 0$."] [17592186069152 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/468/Source/Images/q-31015.png)\n\nGiven the graph above, solve the inequality $- (x - 2)(x - 4) > 0$."] [17592186068509 :question/problem "Given the graph below, solve the inequality $(x+2)(1-x) \\geq 0$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/468/Source/Images/7f86e2d3365b5b2d8c7d4529af5e4b74.png)"] [17592186068509 :question/worked-solution "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n(x+2)(1-x) \\geq 0\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny = (x+2)(1-x)\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/468/Source/Images/210002d3cf31f38ff05cfb4d2c8facd8.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is\n\n$$\n-2 \\leq x \\leq 1\n$$"] [17592186068598 :question/problem "Given the graph below, solve the inequality $-x^2+2x+3 \\leq 0$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/468/Source/Images/e5447e5aa012a36be7ea03184d2d92e7.png)"] [17592186068598 :question/worked-solution "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n-x^2+2x+3 \\leq 0\n$$\n\nis a \"*less than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny =-x^2+2x+3\n$$\n\nis *below* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/468/Source/Images/0dd92f7bab40acea832ee8b4ca514994.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is\n\n$$\nx \\leq -1\n$$\n\nor\n\n$$\nx \\geq 3\n$$"] [17592186068599 :question/problem "Given the graph below, solve the inequality $-(x+2)(x-1) < 0$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/468/Source/Images/204af430d9ba7f6fa3f62a4c2abb7879.png)"] [17592186068599 :question/worked-solution "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n-(x+2)(x-1) < 0\n$$\n\nis a \"*less than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny = -(x+2)(x-1)\n$$\n\nis *below* the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/468/Source/Images/75f69e4ae829fa9d8e57646ed3e3d4bf.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x< -2$ or $x > 1$."] [17592186068597 :question/problem "Given the graph below, solve the inequality $x^2- 3x-10 >0$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/468/Source/Images/c26583fa9f6c7acbaccf7857b267dc1c.png)"] [17592186068597 :question/worked-solution "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\nx^2 -3x -10> 0\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola\n\n$$\ny =x^2 -3x -10\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/468/Source/Images/3f7b1ac593e390153a762ca37cf339f6.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x < -2$ or $x > 5$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186066185 17592186066186 17592186066187 17592186066188 17592186066189 17592186066452 17592186066453 17592186066454 17592186066455 17592186066456] "immutable_fields" [[17592186066184 :answer-field/correct] [17592186066184 :answer-field/id] [17592186066184 :answer-field/key] [17592186066184 :answer-field/type] [17592186066451 :answer-field/correct] [17592186066451 :answer-field/id] [17592186066451 :answer-field/key] [17592186066451 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
